Z||000000||1986 Fiero||03-23-2001||03:11 PM||||Ok my 86 2.5L use to idle at 25-30 before i changed the oil now at idle it is at about 40,but when i am in drive and stopped at a light it goes down to about 20 sometimes even lower but when i give it gas it goes back to 40 but has not yet went any higher then 40.Does anyone know what could be wrong?Also my car only has 74,000 original miles.<BR>             Thanks Alot||||reg||1
Z||000001||Voytek||03-23-2001||05:24 PM||||What do you mean it used to idle at 25-30?  PSI?  I guess canadan Fieros have a readout in kPa.  It could be your oil sending unit.  Other than that I don't know - sorry.  As long as your dipstick shows you have oil, you're fine!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||03-23-2001||06:15 PM||||You changed viscosity...<BR>  I run 10W-30, as 5W-30 is too light...<BR>If you still have low idle pressure, try 15W-40...<BR>As the oil heats, it gets lighter in viscosity, which causes low pressure at idle...<P>||||reg||1
